#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Hakbang 1: Imapa ang mga klasikal na input sa isang quantum na problema {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Graph &rarr; Hamiltonian {#graph-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Graph &rarr; Hamiltonian {#graph-hamiltonian}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, map the problem onto a quantum circuit that is suited for the QAOA. Details on this process can be found in the [introductory QAOA tutorial](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm).\n"
msgstr "Una, imapa ang problema sa isang quantum circuit na angkop para sa QAOA. Ang mga detalye ng prosesong ito ay makikita sa [panimulang QAOA tutorial](/tutorials/quantum-approximate-optimization-algorithm).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/8b864d32-9483-45ea-831f-60488e330adb-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/8b864d32-9483-45ea-831f-60488e330adb-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagpapatakbo sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "SWAP strategy with the SAT initial mapping {#swap-strategy-with-the-sat-initial-mapping}"
msgstr "Estratehiya ng SWAP na may SAT initial mapping {#swap-strategy-with-the-sat-initial-mapping}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We will demonstrate how to build and optimize QAOA circuits using the **SWAP strategy with SAT initial mapping**, a specifically designed transpiler pass for QAOA applied to quadratic problems.\n"
msgstr "Ipapakita namin kung paano bumuo at mag-optimize ng mga QAOA circuit gamit ang **estratehiya ng SWAP na may SAT initial mapping**, isang transpiler pass na espesyal na dinisenyo para sa QAOA na inilalapat sa mga quadratic na problema.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this example, we choose a SWAP insertion strategy for blocks of commuting two-qubit gates, which applies layers of SWAP gates that are simultaneously executable on the coupling map. This strategy is presented in [\\[1\\]](#references) and is passed into `Commuting2qGateRouter`, which is exposed as a standardized Qiskit transpiler pass (see [`Commuting2qGateRouter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Commuting2qGateRouter)). We use a line swap strategy in this example.\n"
msgstr "Sa halimbawang ito, pumipili kami ng estratehiya sa paglalagay ng SWAP para sa mga bloke ng nagko-commute na two-qubit gate, na naglalapat ng mga layer ng SWAP gate na maaaring isagawa nang sabay-sabay sa coupling map. Ang estratehiyang ito ay ipinakita sa [\\[1\\]](#references) at ipinasok sa `Commuting2qGateRouter`, na inilalabas bilang isang standardisadong Qiskit transpiler pass (tingnan ang [`Commuting2qGateRouter`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.passes.Commuting2qGateRouter)). Gumagamit kami ng line swap strategy sa halimbawang ito.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Remap the graph using a SAT mapper {#remap-the-graph-using-a-sat-mapper}"
msgstr "I-remap ang graph gamit ang SAT mapper {#remap-the-graph-using-a-sat-mapper}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Even when a circuit consists of commuting gates (this is the case for the QAOA circuit, but also for Trotterized simulations of Ising Hamiltonians), finding a good initial mapping is a challenging task. When we use the SAT-based approach presented in [\\[2\\]](#references), we can discover effective initial mappings for circuits with commuting gates, resulting in a significant reduction in the number of required SWAP layers. This approach has been demonstrated to scale to up to *500 qubits*, as illustrated in the paper.\n"
msgstr "Kahit na ang isang circuit ay binubuo ng mga nagko-commute na gate (ganito ang kaso para sa QAOA circuit, gayundin para sa mga Trotterized na simulation ng Ising Hamiltonians), ang paghanap ng magandang initial mapping ay isang mahirap na gawain. Kapag ginamit natin ang SAT-based na pamamaraan na ipinakita sa [\\[2\\]](#references), maaari tayong matuklasan ang mga epektibong initial mapping para sa mga circuit na may nagko-commute na gate, na nagresulta sa malaking pagbaba sa bilang ng mga kinakailangang SWAP layer. Ipinakita na ang pamamaraang ito na kaya nitong suportahan ang hanggang *500 qubit*, tulad ng ilustrasyon sa papel.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following code demonstrates how to use the `SATMapper` from Matsuo et al. to remap the graph. This process allows the problem to be mapped to a more optimal initial state for a specified SWAP strategy, resulting in a significant reduction in the number of SWAP layers required to execute the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod na code ay nagpapakita kung paano gamitin ang `SATMapper` mula kay Matsuo et al. para i-remap ang graph. Pinapahintulutan ng prosesong ito na mai-map ang problema sa mas optimal na initial state para sa isang tinukoy na estratehiya ng SWAP, na nagresulta sa malaking pagbaba sa bilang ng mga SWAP layer na kinakailangan upang mapatakbo ang circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In `SATMapper`, the problem of finding a good initial mapping is formulated as a SAT problem. A SAT solver is used to find such an initial mapping for the QAOA circuit. `python-sat` (`pysat` for short) is a Python library for a SAT solver, and we will use it to solve the SAT problem in this example.\n"
msgstr "Sa `SATMapper`, ang problema ng paghanap ng magandang initial mapping ay binalangkas bilang isang SAT na problema. Ginagamit ang SAT solver upang mahanap ang ganoong initial mapping para sa QAOA circuit. Ang `python-sat` (o `pysat` para sa maikli) ay isang Python library para sa isang SAT solver, at gagamitin namin ito upang malutas ang SAT na problema sa halimbawang ito.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/e689e09e-6ca7-4154-8602-d1d954ebe80b-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/e689e09e-6ca7-4154-8602-d1d954ebe80b-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a QAOA circuit with the SWAP strategy and the SAT mapping {#build-a-qaoa-circuit-with-the-swap-strategy-and-the-sat-mapping}"
msgstr "Bumuo ng QAOA circuit gamit ang estratehiya ng SWAP at ang SAT mapping {#build-a-qaoa-circuit-with-the-swap-strategy-and-the-sat-mapping}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We only want to apply the SWAP strategies to the cost operator layer, so we start by creating the isolated block that we will later transform and append to the final QAOA circuit.\n"
msgstr "Nais lamang naming ilapat ang mga estratehiya ng SWAP sa layer ng cost operator, kaya nagsisimula kami sa pamamagitan ng paglikha ng hiwalay na bloke na babaguhin namin at ilalakip sa panghuling QAOA circuit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For this, we can use the [`QAOAAnsatz`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.QAOAAnsatz) class from Qiskit. We input an empty circuit to the `initial_state` and `mixer_operator` fields to make sure we are building an isolated cost operator layer.\n"
"We also define the `edge_coloring` map so that RZZ gates are positioned next to SWAP gates. This strategic placement allows us to exploit CX cancellations, optimizing the circuit for better performance.\n"
"This process is executed within the `create_qaoa_swap_circuit` function.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para dito, maaari naming gamitin ang klase ng [`QAOAAnsatz`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.QAOAAnsatz) mula sa Qiskit. Naglalagay kami ng walang laman na circuit sa mga field na `initial_state` at `mixer_operator` upang matiyak na nagtatayo kami ng hiwalay na layer ng cost operator.\n"
"Tinutukoy din namin ang mapa ng `edge_coloring` upang ang mga RZZ gate ay nakaposisyon katabi ng mga SWAP gate. Ang estratehikong paglalagay na ito ay nagbibigay-daan sa amin na samantalahin ang mga CX cancellation, na nag-o-optimize ng circuit para sa mas magandang pagganap.\n"
"Ang prosesong ito ay isinasagawa sa loob ng function na `create_qaoa_swap_circuit`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/82ae28b3-85eb-4487-8100-1e622e93cccf-1.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/82ae28b3-85eb-4487-8100-1e622e93cccf-1.avif)\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using IBM Quantum primitives {#step-3-execute-using-ibm-quantum-primitives}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Isagawa gamit ang mga IBM Quantum primitive {#step-3-execute-using-ibm-quantum-primitives}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's now prepare for hardware execution. Our first step will be to define a  Conditional Value at Risk (CVaR) cost function, which was introduced in [\\[3\\]](#references) for use within the paradigm of variational quantum optimization algorithms.\n"
msgstr "Ihanda na natin para sa pagpapatakbo sa hardware. Ang aming unang hakbang ay tukuyin ang isang Conditional Value at Risk (CVaR) cost function, na ipinakikilala sa [\\[3\\]](#references) para sa paggamit sa loob ng paradigma ng mga variational quantum optimization algorithm.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CVaR of a random variable $X$ for a confidence level $α ∈ (0, 1]$ is defined as\n"
"$CVaR_{\\alpha}(X) = \\mathbb{E} \\lbrack X | X \\leq F_X^{-1}(\\alpha) \\rbrack$\n"
"where $F_X^{-1}(p)$ is the inverse cumulative distribution function of $X$. In other words, CVaR is the expected value of the lower $\\alpha$-tail of the distribution of $X$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang CVaR ng isang random variable na $X$ para sa confidence level na $α ∈ (0, 1]$ ay tinukoy bilang\n"
"$CVaR_{\\alpha}(X) = \\mathbb{E} \\lbrack X | X \\leq F_X^{-1}(\\alpha) \\rbrack$\n"
"kung saan ang $F_X^{-1}(p)$ ay ang inverse cumulative distribution function ng $X$. Sa madaling salita, ang CVaR ay ang inaasahang halaga ng mas mababang $\\alpha$-tail ng distribusyon ng $X$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The CVaR can be used as an error mitigation technique as previously discussed [\\[4\\]](#references). In this example, we determine $\\alpha$ and the number of shots according to the [error per layered gate](/guides/qpu-information#2q-error-layered) (EPLG) associated with the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring gamitin ang CVaR bilang isang teknik sa pagpapababa ng error tulad ng dati nang tinalakay [\\[4\\]](#references). Sa halimbawang ito, tinutukoy namin ang $\\alpha$ at ang bilang ng mga shot ayon sa [error per layered gate](/guides/qpu-information#2q-error-layered) (EPLG) na nauugnay sa circuit.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process at ibalik ang resulta sa nais na klasikal na format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's now visualize our results and then post-process them to find the value of the cut.\n"
msgstr "I-visualize na natin ang ating mga resulta at pagkatapos ay i-post-process ang mga ito upang mahanap ang halaga ng cut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/761821cb-9a0c-4efb-806b-75513302d34a-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/advanced-techniques-for-qaoa/extracted-outputs/761821cb-9a0c-4efb-806b-75513302d34a-0.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following retrieves the best solution from the sampled bitstrings:\n"
msgstr "Kinukuha ng sumusunod ang pinakamahusay na solusyon mula sa mga na-sample na bitstring\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider the Hamiltonian $H_C$ for the **max-cut** problem. Let each vertex of the graph be associated with a qubit in state $|0\\rangle$ or $|1\\rangle$, where the value denotes the set the vertex is in. The goal of the problem is to maximize the number of edges $(v_1, v_2)$ for which $v_1 = |0\\rangle$ and $v_2 = |1\\rangle$, or vice versa. If we associate the $Z$ operator with each qubit, where\n"
msgstr "Isaalang-alang ang Hamiltonian na $H_C$ para sa problemang **Max-Cut**. Hayaan ang bawat vertex ng graph na maugnay sa isang qubit sa estado na $|0\\rangle$ o $|1\\rangle$, kung saan ang halaga ay nagpapahiwatig ng set na kinabibilangan ng vertex. Ang layunin ng problema ay i-maximize ang bilang ng mga gilid $(v_1, v_2)$ kung saan ang $v_1 = |0\\rangle$ at $v_2 = |1\\rangle$, o kabaligtaran. Kung iuugnay natin ang operator na $Z$ sa bawat qubit, kung saan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"    Z|0\\rangle = |0\\rangle \\qquad Z|1\\rangle = -|1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"    Z|0\\rangle = |0\\rangle \\qquad Z|1\\rangle = -|1\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "then an edge $(v_1, v_2)$ belongs to the cut if the eigenvalue of $(Z_1|v_1\\rangle) \\cdot (Z_2|v_2\\rangle) = -1$; in other words, the qubits associated with $v_1$ and $v_2$ are different. Similarly, $(v_1, v_2)$ does not belong to the cut if the eigenvalue of $(Z_1|v_1\\rangle) \\cdot (Z_2|v_2\\rangle) = 1$.\n"
msgstr "kung gayon ang isang gilid $(v_1, v_2)$ ay kabilang sa cut kung ang eigenvalue ng $(Z_1|v_1\\rangle) \\cdot (Z_2|v_2\\rangle) = -1$; sa madaling salita, ang mga qubit na nauugnay sa $v_1$ at $v_2$ ay magkaiba. Gayundin, ang $(v_1, v_2)$ ay hindi kabilang sa cut kung ang eigenvalue ng $(Z_1|v_1\\rangle) \\cdot (Z_2|v_2\\rangle) = 1$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, let's draw a graph based on the CVaR result.\n"
"We split the graph nodes into two sets based on the CVaR result.\n"
"The nodes in the first set are colored in gray, and the nodes in the second set are colored in purple.\n"
"The edges between the two sets are the edges that are cut by the partitioning.\n"
msgstr ""
"Panghuli, gumawa tayo ng graph batay sa resulta ng CVaR.\n"
"Hinahati natin ang mga node ng graph sa dalawang set batay sa resulta ng CVaR.\n"
"Ang mga node sa unang set ay may kulay na gray, at ang mga node sa ikalawang set ay may kulay na purple.\n"
"Ang mga gilid sa pagitan ng dalawang set ay ang mga gilid na hinahati ng partisyon.\n"

